{
  "id": "utility.lottery",
  "title": "Lottery",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "utility/utility_lottery.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Lottery</h1>\n<p>For a finite set of outcomes $O$, a lottery is a probability distribution on\n$O$. The degenerate lottery at $o\\in O$ assigns probability one to $o$.</p>\n<p>Given lotteries $L_1,L_2$ and a scalar $\\alpha\\in[0,1]$, the compound lottery\n$$\n  [\\alpha L_1,(1-\\alpha)L_2]\n$$\nis the lottery assigning each outcome the probability\n$$\n  \\alpha L_1(o)+(1-\\alpha)L_2(o).\n$$</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
